{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>HaShem your Elohim has allotted them to all the peoples.</b> He arranged them in a fitting order for the needs of each region of the earth, according to the variation of each region and the variation of the people dwelling in it. And this perceptible order demonstrates the opposite of the views of those who stray, for it necessarily indicates that there exists some being who arranges them toward a directed end — He who brought them into being to order them, so that the purpose of their existence and arrangement may be attained. For all this cannot be by chance, without doubt."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:26.907734948Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}